    },
    {
      "type": "p",
      "md": "Per side, the book is an ordered map price -> FIFO deque of remaining quantities. Ordered maps keep prices sorted, so the best ask is begin() on the ask map and the best bid is begin() on a bid map ordered with a greater comparator (or rbegin() on an ascending map). The deque per level preserves arrival order; its front element is the order that time priority trades first."
    },
    {
      "type": "steps",
      "title": "Sweeping with a market order",
      "items": [
        "Take the opposite side's map; let best = its best key while the map is non-empty.",
        "front = quantity of the front order at best; fill = min(front, remaining market qty). Emit T best fill (formatted from cents).",
        "If fill == front, pop the front order; if its level deque is now empty, erase the price level entirely. Otherwise reduce the front element to front, fill; it stays at the head of the queue.",
        "Re-read best (the map may have changed) and repeat while market qty > 0 and the side is non-empty."
      ]
    },
